text:
Use `pg` pool. Config:

```js
import { Pool } from 'pg';

const pool = new Pool({
  connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL,

  // Pool size
  max: 20,                // max connections
  min: 2,                 // keep alive when idle
  idleTimeoutMillis: 30_000,     // kill idle conn after 30s
  connectionTimeoutMillis: 5_000, // fail fast if can't connect in 5s
  allowExitOnIdle: true,         // let process exit cleanly
});

// Test on startup
pool.connect()
  .then(client => { client.release(); console.log('DB ready'); })
  .catch(err => { console.error('DB connect fail:', err); process.exit(1); });

// Catch pool-level errors (e.g. dropped conn)
pool.on('error', (err) => {
  console.error('Idle client error:', err);
});
```

Query wrapper — auto-release, timeout per query:

```js
async function query(sql, params, timeoutMs = 10_000) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    await client.query(`SET statement_timeout = ${timeoutMs}`);
    return await client.query(sql, params);
  } finally {
    client.release();  // always release, even on throw
  }
}
```

Transaction wrapper:

```js
async function withTransaction(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    await client.query('BEGIN');
    const result = await fn(client);
    await client.query('COMMIT');
    return result;
  } catch (err) {
    await client.query('ROLLBACK');
    throw err;
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}

// Usage
await withTransaction(async (client) => {
  await client.query('UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - $1 WHERE id = $2', [100, 1]);
  await client.query('UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + $1 WHERE id = $2', [100, 2]);
});
```

Shutdown:

```js
process.on('SIGTERM', async () => {
  await pool.end();  // drain pool, close all conn
  process.exit(0);
});
```

Key numbers:

| Setting | Prod | Dev |
|---|---|---|
| `max` | 10–20 | 2–5 |
| `idleTimeoutMillis` | 30k | 10k |
| `connectionTimeoutMillis` | 5k | 2k |
| `statement_timeout` | 10–30k | 5k |

`max` cap = DB `max_connections` ÷ app instances. Leave headroom for migrations/admin.
